# Keep one line-ending convention in the repo.
#
# This repo had no attributes while `core.autocrlf=true` was set, so the same
# file could be CRLF in the working copy and LF in the index — which produced
# spurious "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings and mixed-ending files when a
# tool rewrote one (both happened during the 2026-10 rename work). Normalising
# to LF in the repository makes the working copy deterministic.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells need CRLF to run reliably.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.tar.gz binary
